message: >-
  If you use daedalus-flow in academic work, please cite it using this
  metadata. See the "How to cite" section of the README.
title: "daedalus-flow"
abstract: >-
  daedalus-flow (the dae command) is a reproducible analysis-pipeline framework,
  "labs of modules", for data-intensive science, with a focus on astronomy and
  exoplanet / space-science workflows.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Patricio
    family-names: Reller
    affiliation: "Centre for Data Intensive Science and Industry (DISI), Department of Physics and Astronomy, University College London"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3161-9239"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-01"
license: Apache-2.0
url: "https://github.com/preller/daedalus-flow"
repository-code: "https://github.com/preller/daedalus-flow"
keywords:
  - reproducibility
  - data pipeline
  - workflow
  - astronomy
  - exoplanets
